# Pairs with InFlightBaseSurvives. Production before the fix (#5357): an
# incremental capture read its base once, before it drained, and published
# without looking at the base again, so a pass that pruned the base during
# the drain left the catalog listing an increment whose base was gone.
MODULE: InFlightBaseSurvivesNoBaseRecheck
TARGET: InFlightBaseSurvives
CLASS: Action
SUMMARY: an increment publishes without re-reading its base's catalog row
PERTURBS: Check

--- FIND
                    IF m.kind = "full" \/ m.base \in cat THEN "ok" ELSE "abandon"]
--- REPLACE
                    \* MUTATION: no re-check of the base before publishing.
                    "ok"]
--- END